WEBVTT

00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:27.870
All right, the Trans-America
Wild Race is about to start!

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:29.200
The rules are simple--

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:32.580
you drive your car from here
in Los Angeles across the country,

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:37.080
and the one who is the fastest
to arrive in New York is the winner!

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:41.870
The first day is a pre-race,
with a prize of $10,000 on the line!

00:00:42.830 --> 00:00:47.500
The daredevil challengers competing
in this unprecedented survival race

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:52.080
are impatiently waiting for
the start signal to be given!

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:57.660
Aren't you ready yet, Appare?! The race
is about to start! What are you doing?!

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:02.080
Final tuning. I'm hurrying. Keep quiet.

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:05.620
Sheesh, we're the only ones doing it.

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:08.500
Kosame, settle down. We have far to go.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:10.500
You're a child; you be quiet.

00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:25.700
Appare, I'm going on ahead!

00:01:29.410 --> 00:01:32.410
You've known for a long time that
today was the start of the race, right?

00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:34.870
Why didn't you have this finished yesterday?!

00:01:34.870 --> 00:01:36.370
--Done.
--Oh, good.

00:01:36.370 --> 00:01:38.660
Hurry, hurry, hurry!

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:39.500
Hototo...

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:40.580
Right.

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:45.580
Hitch up your loincloth, Kosame.

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:48.910
Huh? D-Drive safely...

00:01:48.910 --> 00:01:54.750
So, let's go and see where this road leads!

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:57.500
Here we go!

00:01:59.290 --> 00:02:00.830
Whoa!

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:06.410
Be careful, everyone.

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:33.620
There you are, Appare. Race me!

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:35.450
I'm not going to hold back!

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:37.830
Hmph, interesting guy.

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:42.910
Kosame, Hototo, hang on! We're gonna
blast out of here as fast as we can go!

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:27.660
"Episode 1"
"Sunny [Appare],
With Occasional Showers [Kosame]"

00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:32.120
"One year earlier"
So you know what my boy did...?

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:32.830
The steam pressure I can estimate
from my experiment results

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:34.660
"Fuyutsuki Prefecture, Yukinoshita Village"
The steam pressure I can estimate
from my experiment results

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:37.370
"Fuyutsuki Prefecture, Yukinoshita Village"
was about 65% of what I expected.

00:04:37.370 --> 00:04:41.500
To get the thermal conductivity to the boiler
to approximate my design calculations,

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:44.410
I'll need to readjust the heat pipe.

00:04:44.410 --> 00:04:47.910
How much clearance between
the pipe and the boiler will be enough?

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:50.910
I guess I'll need to reexamine
the cooling system

00:04:50.910 --> 00:04:54.080
to see how long I can extend
its practical running time.

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:56.580
There's still some room for improvement.

00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:03.200
Next!

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:05.370
Big Brother!

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:07.370
Big Brother!

00:05:07.370 --> 00:05:08.410
What is it, Fumi?

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:11.410
Where are your manners? Also, in the dojo...

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:14.330
--...address me as "Shihandai."
--...address me as "Shihandai."

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:18.500
Shihandai, a messenger
from Lord Kuroda has arrived,

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:20.950
and says that you are to come
to his mansion immediately.

00:05:20.950 --> 00:05:24.000
What?! Why didn't you say so?!

00:05:26.750 --> 00:05:29.330
You know Sorano Appare, right?

00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:31.410
The Sorano family's second son?

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:32.910
Yes, sir.

00:05:32.910 --> 00:05:34.580
He's a genius when it comes to gadgets,

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:37.870
and creates the most unusual things,
under the guise of being experiments.

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:41.700
Rumor has it that he carries on
in some rather wild behavior.

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:43.700
They are not rumors!

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:46.200
Wha--?!

00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:48.910
What is that?

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:52.870
I don't know! But look at my treasured garden!

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:54.660
If this were the Tokugawa Era,

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:57.790
I would slay him for this insolence,
no questions asked.

00:05:57.790 --> 00:05:58.700
Huh?

00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:00.540
But though they are commoners,

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:04.700
their family were major merchants
who once even dealt with the shogunate.

00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:07.700
If I'm not careful,
this could blow up in <i>my </i>face.

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:11.330
Yes, quite right.
The fellow is trouble, all right.

00:06:11.330 --> 00:06:16.000
Which brings me to you, Kosame.
I'm ordering you to be Appare's overseer.

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:17.830
Huh? Me?!

00:06:17.830 --> 00:06:20.790
You're close to his age. It's the perfect fit.

00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:23.160
The perfect fit for what, sir?

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:27.540
Also, from what I hear,
he was once a pupil at your dojo.

00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:31.750
Oh, no, sir, his father
twisted my arm to let him join,

00:06:31.750 --> 00:06:33.750
but I expelled him within three days--

00:06:33.750 --> 00:06:35.540
I am done talking!

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:39.160
If anything else happens,
you will be jointly responsible.

00:06:39.160 --> 00:06:41.040
Keep a tight watch over him.

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:42.700
Yes, sir.

00:06:42.700 --> 00:06:47.700
Then again, he may have already
been killed inside the jail by now.

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:48.790
Huh?

00:06:48.790 --> 00:06:51.620
I had him thrown into the major criminals cell.

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:54.200
If he dies in a run-in with another criminal,

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:56.910
no one will have to accept any blame.

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:02.540
Hey, new guy, too good to say hello?

00:07:02.540 --> 00:07:05.330
I don't say hello. Waste of time.

00:07:05.330 --> 00:07:08.750
Wh-What?! Why, you...!

00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:10.040
Move your foot.

00:07:10.040 --> 00:07:13.200
Ha, why don't you go ahead and make me?

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:17.790
Ee-yow!

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:19.120
What the hell was that for?!

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:22.080
--My foot...!
--He told me to, didn't he?

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:25.620
You've got some attitude.

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:28.750
Let me teach you the rules in here.

00:07:28.750 --> 00:07:29.950
That won't be necessary.

00:07:29.950 --> 00:07:30.870
Huh?

00:07:30.870 --> 00:07:32.410
I'm leaving now.

00:07:42.750 --> 00:07:47.080
H-Hey, wait! Open it up
once again! Hey! Come back!

00:07:47.080 --> 00:07:49.370
Hey, they're raising a racket.

00:07:49.370 --> 00:07:50.790
Let them be.

00:07:50.790 --> 00:07:53.750
We're on notice to pretend not to
see anything, no matter what happens.

00:07:53.750 --> 00:07:55.000
Right.

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:04.120
Huh? There was one other,
wasn't there? A sassy little brat.

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:05.870
He got the hell out.

00:08:05.870 --> 00:08:07.040
Huh?

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:12.080
"Sorano's"

00:08:18.330 --> 00:08:19.700
Appare!

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:21.040
Where have you been?!

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:25.540
The beach. After that, I broke into
an estate, got put in jail,

00:08:25.540 --> 00:08:27.290
and now I've come home.

00:08:27.290 --> 00:08:31.040
What exactly do you think you're doing?!

00:08:31.040 --> 00:08:33.830
You wouldn't even understand it
if I explained it to you.

00:08:33.830 --> 00:08:38.580
Appare! You can't talk to your father like that!

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:42.620
You're 19 years old now.
Stop wasting your time with nonsense

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:44.660
and help out with the household business!

00:08:44.660 --> 00:08:47.450
Just because you're the second son,
I won't have you messing around!

00:08:47.450 --> 00:08:51.330
I'm busy right now. I have other things to do.

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:54.080
If you aren't going to work, then get out!

00:08:57.040 --> 00:09:00.830
The thing is, he opened the jail door
on his own and walked away.

00:09:00.830 --> 00:09:05.120
Escaping from jail is a serious offense.
Gather some men!

00:09:05.120 --> 00:09:08.830
We'll catch him, and make sure he
can't ever pull his foolishness again!

00:09:08.830 --> 00:09:10.040
--Yes, sir!
--Yes, sir!

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:18.290
Damn it!

00:09:18.290 --> 00:09:20.370
He's such a handful!

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:25.330
"Measure of Last Resort"

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:26.660
"Measure of Last Resort"
All right...

00:09:26.660 --> 00:09:28.870
"Measure of Last Resort"
What do you need your katana for?

00:09:28.870 --> 00:09:31.750
"Measure of Last Resort"
To catch a criminal.

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:33.370
"Measure of Last Resort"
Is everything okay?

00:09:33.370 --> 00:09:36.790
Yeah. I'll handle this before
things get out of hand.

00:09:36.790 --> 00:09:38.540
Huh?

00:09:38.540 --> 00:09:43.250
Hey, don't worry. I'll be back in no time.

00:09:43.250 --> 00:09:46.370
Ah...! Aw, man...

00:09:46.370 --> 00:09:46.660
"Sorano's"
Ah...! Aw, man...

00:09:46.660 --> 00:09:49.790
"Sorano's"
Pardon me, but is Appare in?

00:09:49.790 --> 00:09:52.790
You're the Shihandai from the Hangetsu Dojo.

00:09:52.790 --> 00:09:56.290
I'm his older brother, Hanbei.
Has he done something again?

00:09:56.290 --> 00:09:58.370
Ah, yes, sort of...

00:09:58.370 --> 00:10:01.200
For crying out loud, he never does any work,

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:03.290
and spends all day tinkering with his devices!

00:10:03.290 --> 00:10:04.370
So, um...

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:09.040
Right. He's in an old storehouse.
Please head around back outside.

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:10.080
Much obliged.

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:11.620
He's good for absolutely nothing around here,

00:10:11.620 --> 00:10:12.250
"Sorano's"
He's good for absolutely nothing around here,

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:16.290
"Sorano's"
so if you would, please tell him
to at least not bother others!

00:10:17.450 --> 00:10:21.700
Appare! I know you're in there! Appare!

00:10:21.700 --> 00:10:23.080
I'm coming in!

00:10:27.950 --> 00:10:30.910
Oh, tea. Isn't that thoughtful?

00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:49.330
The explosion is still too late, huh?

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:52.290
The internal steam pressure
could use a little tweaking.

00:10:52.290 --> 00:10:54.950
Hey, hold on!

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:01.160
What is this place?

00:11:07.250 --> 00:11:09.830
A western technical manual?

00:11:09.830 --> 00:11:13.160
It's not a technical manual; it's a story.

00:11:13.160 --> 00:11:14.540
A story?

00:11:14.540 --> 00:11:17.000
No touching. Who are you?

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:19.620
Have you forgotten who I am?!

00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:22.000
When you enrolled at my dojo three years ago,

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:24.540
and used that underhanded weapon on me...

00:11:31.660 --> 00:11:33.040
<i>Men</i>.

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:35.000
Yeah, you're that guy who lost to me.

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:37.000
That did not count as a loss!

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:40.700
And these days, I am a Shihandai
of the Hangetsu Ittoryu School.

00:11:40.700 --> 00:11:42.410
Oh, but this isn't the time.

00:11:42.410 --> 00:11:45.660
There are men out there
gathering right now to arrest you.

00:11:45.660 --> 00:11:47.620
The way things are looking,
they'll have your head.

00:11:47.620 --> 00:11:50.790
I will help you beg them
to at least spare your life,

00:11:50.790 --> 00:11:53.160
so you have to turn yourself
back in at the jail.

00:11:53.160 --> 00:11:54.040
Nope.

00:11:54.040 --> 00:11:54.910
Wha--?

00:11:54.910 --> 00:11:56.250
It's no fun in there.

00:11:56.250 --> 00:12:01.330
No fun...? Listen, you, it's not
a question of being fun or not.

00:12:01.330 --> 00:12:02.910
Then what is it a question of?

00:12:02.910 --> 00:12:07.660
Huh? Well, you know, it's... it's...

00:12:07.660 --> 00:12:10.410
Either way, they're going to
catch you like this!

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:14.250
Suit yourself. I'm going to do
whatever <i>I </i>want to.

00:12:14.250 --> 00:12:18.830
Look, you... Stop being so inconsiderate!

00:12:18.830 --> 00:12:22.120
You may think that, but who says it like that?

00:12:22.120 --> 00:12:25.700
Now's the time to start to panic,
and beg for your life, right?

00:12:25.700 --> 00:12:28.410
I'm trying to reach out and save you, here.

00:12:28.410 --> 00:12:29.790
I never asked you.

00:12:30.790 --> 00:12:35.200
I'm also responsible, since I was
ordered to be your overseer.

00:12:36.700 --> 00:12:41.950
If that's your attitude, then I cannot
afford to leave you like this, either.

00:12:45.370 --> 00:12:48.330
Please! I'm begging you!

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:51.620
You have to come with me,
and apologize to Lord Kuroda!

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:55.410
I still have an unmarried younger sister
and an elderly father!

00:12:55.410 --> 00:12:58.250
I can't afford to answer for you with my life!

00:12:58.250 --> 00:13:01.290
Please! Please try to see reason!

00:13:01.290 --> 00:13:04.500
Incidentally, my father has
arranged a wife for me.

00:13:04.500 --> 00:13:09.660
I haven't met her yet, but I'm sure
she's a beautiful, well-tempered girl.

00:13:09.660 --> 00:13:13.040
I can't very well widow her
before we even get married!

00:13:13.040 --> 00:13:15.660
--Come on! Come on!
--Stop, already!

00:13:15.660 --> 00:13:19.450
I've had a lot of people try to get me
to bow down to them before,

00:13:19.450 --> 00:13:22.040
but you're the first one to bow to me.

00:13:22.040 --> 00:13:23.870
It's making my skin crawl.

00:13:23.870 --> 00:13:25.790
Then, does that mean you'll come with me?

00:13:25.790 --> 00:13:27.830
No, I won't do that.

00:13:27.830 --> 00:13:29.620
In exchange, I have a favor to ask.

00:13:29.620 --> 00:13:32.290
Huh? In exchange for what?

00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:34.910
"Sorano's"

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:37.870
Excuse me! Is Sorano Appare here?!

00:13:37.870 --> 00:13:40.330
Yes. Is there something you needed?

00:13:40.330 --> 00:13:44.500
We're hauling Appare in! It won't
end well for you if you try to hide him!

00:13:47.790 --> 00:13:50.870
Where are we going, for heaven's sake?

00:14:04.620 --> 00:14:06.330
Where are we?

00:14:07.500 --> 00:14:09.000
My ship's dock.

00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:10.330
Dock?

00:14:10.330 --> 00:14:12.080
I'm building a steamship here.

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:17.040
A steamship? You can build
something like this by yourself?

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:22.620
Yeah. Ever since we got the new government,
it's been easier to get foreign books and parts.

00:14:22.620 --> 00:14:26.160
They have just about anything
if you go to the shipyard in Nagasaki.

00:14:26.160 --> 00:14:31.580
That's fine and all, but does it work?
It's pretty small for a steamship.

00:14:31.580 --> 00:14:35.200
Yeah. That's what's new about this engine.

00:14:35.200 --> 00:14:37.500
It has the same horsepower, but shrunk down.

00:14:37.500 --> 00:14:41.250
Once it's finished, it's possible it
could be the fastest ship in the world.

00:14:41.250 --> 00:14:43.330
In the world?!

00:14:44.330 --> 00:14:48.790
You're such a dreamer! Your brother
was worried about you, too.

00:14:48.790 --> 00:14:51.750
You should do some honest work,
and put your parents' minds at ease--

00:14:51.750 --> 00:14:52.830
You're the same.

00:14:52.830 --> 00:14:54.120
Huh?

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:58.040
I thought you might be
a little different, but sure enough,

00:14:58.040 --> 00:15:00.580
you're just like my old man and my brother.

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:02.290
How so?

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:04.910
Just go away. I'm leaving.

00:15:04.910 --> 00:15:06.160
Leaving?

00:15:10.370 --> 00:15:11.660
There.

00:15:14.330 --> 00:15:16.540
Hmm? H-Hey...

00:15:16.540 --> 00:15:19.160
Think about this. Stop for a minute.

00:15:19.160 --> 00:15:21.580
Appare!

00:15:21.580 --> 00:15:22.950
Big Sister?

00:15:24.540 --> 00:15:25.950
What's up?

00:15:25.950 --> 00:15:30.370
A lot of officers just came to the house.
They're looking for you.

00:15:30.370 --> 00:15:33.910
Aw, didn't I tell you so?

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:36.620
Okay. I'm going to head out for a bit.

00:15:36.620 --> 00:15:39.450
Oh... Is everything all right?

00:15:39.450 --> 00:15:41.200
Mm-hmm.

00:15:41.200 --> 00:15:42.620
When are you coming back?

00:15:44.160 --> 00:15:45.910
I think it will be a while.

00:15:47.450 --> 00:15:48.830
I see.

00:15:49.950 --> 00:15:53.750
Well, off you go. Take care of yourself.

00:15:56.290 --> 00:15:58.290
Here.

00:15:58.290 --> 00:16:00.750
Good luck charms are just superstition.

00:16:00.750 --> 00:16:02.910
That's okay.

00:16:02.910 --> 00:16:09.040
Please? Consider it a gesture
to reassure me, and take it.

00:16:12.290 --> 00:16:13.660
Off I go.

00:16:23.200 --> 00:16:27.910
Hey, hello, everyone! Thanks for coming!
I just now spotted Appare.

00:16:27.910 --> 00:16:30.160
You know, he's not really all that bad,

00:16:30.160 --> 00:16:32.330
and I can convince him to turn himself in,

00:16:32.330 --> 00:16:36.500
so can I ask you all to wait here?
There's no need for anything rough--

00:16:36.500 --> 00:16:37.700
Hey...

00:16:37.700 --> 00:16:38.540
Huh?

00:16:38.540 --> 00:16:41.290
Ah! H-Hold on a minute!

00:16:42.660 --> 00:16:45.200
That's dangerous. Are you sure
you wanna do that?

00:16:48.410 --> 00:16:51.450
All right. Suit yourself.

00:16:51.450 --> 00:16:53.120
Okay, let's go.

00:16:54.620 --> 00:16:57.160
Mm-hmm, that sounds great.

00:16:57.160 --> 00:16:58.250
Hey!

00:16:58.250 --> 00:17:00.870
Stop this ship right now and head back!

00:17:00.870 --> 00:17:03.790
I'm going off on a journey.
If you don't want to come, get off.

00:17:03.790 --> 00:17:05.040
A journey?!

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:08.910
Nagasaki, Kobe, Yokohama...
Then I'll cross the ocean and--

00:17:08.910 --> 00:17:11.410
Are you kidding?! I'm going back!

00:17:11.410 --> 00:17:12.620
Oh, hey, let go!

00:17:12.620 --> 00:17:15.660
No, <i>you </i>let go! I'm going back!

00:17:21.500 --> 00:17:23.200
Oh, that's...

00:17:44.660 --> 00:17:47.540
It's hopeless. We have no food or water.

00:17:47.540 --> 00:17:49.000
I already told you that.

00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:53.040
If you were planning to go on a journey,
why didn't you get anything ready?

00:17:53.040 --> 00:17:58.250
I brought everything I needed.
Tools, tech manuals, gadgets for crafting...

00:17:58.250 --> 00:18:00.000
Food and water!

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:03.200
I never planned to come this far out to sea.

00:18:05.080 --> 00:18:06.580
Can you repair it?

00:18:06.580 --> 00:18:10.200
I'm not fixing it,
I'm just checking its condition.

00:18:10.200 --> 00:18:13.200
The emergency acceleration device
was meant to be disposable,

00:18:13.200 --> 00:18:15.330
so it's impossible to repair it here.

00:18:15.330 --> 00:18:18.870
We're also out of fuel.
And the rudder is busted.

00:18:18.870 --> 00:18:22.370
Is there any way we can survive this?

00:18:22.370 --> 00:18:25.290
Taking into account the position of
the stars and our departure location,

00:18:25.290 --> 00:18:27.500
as well as the direction we took off in,

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:30.540
land is most likely in the direction
of the Serpent's watch.

00:18:30.540 --> 00:18:33.410
The ship ran all-out for half a watch.

00:18:33.410 --> 00:18:36.700
Calculating our inertia and direction
the ocean currents have since taken us in,

00:18:36.700 --> 00:18:39.700
as well as how fast we're being carried,

00:18:39.700 --> 00:18:40.540
I would estimate the distance to shore
is between 22 and 25 <i>ri</i>.

00:18:40.540 --> 00:18:43.290
"22 <i>ri </i>~ 25 <i>ri</i>"
I would estimate the distance to shore
is between 22 and 25 <i>ri</i>.

00:18:43.290 --> 00:18:44.000
I would estimate the distance to shore
is between 22 and 25 <i>ri</i>.

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:45.160
Can you swim?

00:18:45.160 --> 00:18:46.910
There's no way I can swim that.

00:18:46.910 --> 00:18:49.830
Same here. Can I get back to work?

00:18:49.830 --> 00:18:51.120
Go ahead.

00:18:54.120 --> 00:19:00.160
What's with you? We could be dead tomorrow.

00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:03.120
How can you be so fixated on that machinery?

00:19:05.540 --> 00:19:07.790
The world is connected.

00:19:07.790 --> 00:19:08.790
Huh?

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:14.870
When I was four, I saw my first steamships.

00:19:14.870 --> 00:19:20.040
I more or less knew that the ocean
was a vastly expansive body of water,

00:19:20.040 --> 00:19:25.370
but there these huge ships I'd never
seen before that came across it.

00:19:25.370 --> 00:19:27.120
Do you get it?

00:19:27.120 --> 00:19:31.370
The ocean that I thought was
just water connected us...

00:19:31.370 --> 00:19:33.450
...to a world I'd never even seen.

00:19:37.660 --> 00:19:40.870
The ocean connects to unknown lands.

00:19:40.870 --> 00:19:45.910
The sky connects to the moon.
The moon connects to the stars.

00:19:45.910 --> 00:19:49.200
This is a story, right? A work of fiction.

00:19:49.200 --> 00:19:51.830
But there is someone
out in the world who thought,

00:19:51.830 --> 00:19:56.370
"What if we could go to the moon?"
Incredible, isn't it?

00:19:57.250 --> 00:20:03.540
How far can I go? Across the sea?
Beyond the sky?

00:20:04.370 --> 00:20:07.830
Or even the other side of the moon?

00:20:10.290 --> 00:20:12.870
The ocean floor, at best.

00:20:18.700 --> 00:20:22.040
If anyone's ever going to reach
the other side of the moon...

00:20:22.040 --> 00:20:25.080
...I'm gonna be the one who gets there first!

00:20:25.080 --> 00:20:27.870
This ship is only the first step.

00:20:28.910 --> 00:20:33.290
Your first step is likely to be your last step.

00:20:56.120 --> 00:21:01.250
Fumi... live a happy life for the both of us...

00:21:12.160 --> 00:21:17.620
So the ferry that takes us across
the Sanzu River... is a steamship?

00:21:17.620 --> 00:21:18.620
Huh?

00:21:37.620 --> 00:21:39.580
Its basic construction is...

00:21:45.000 --> 00:21:47.160
Hey, you get working, too!

00:22:12.620 --> 00:22:16.950
So this is America! Los Angeles!

00:22:16.950 --> 00:22:19.330
Oh my God!

00:23:46.750 --> 00:23:47.370
"Next time"

